  "term": "U.S. Food and Drug Administration",
  "definition": "The U.S. Food and Drug Administration is the United States body described here as approving medications for clinical use, such as esketamine for treatment-resistant depression. In this context, its approval indicates that a drug has been authorized for that treatment use.",
